WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.401
-My first guest is
a very talented actor,

00:00:02.401 --> 00:00:04.237
writer, and director.

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:07.874
She stars alongside Bill Murray
in the movie "On the Rocks,"

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:10.609
which is streaming now
on Apple TV+.

00:00:10.609 --> 00:00:13.646
Here is Rashida Jones!

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:16.515
Ah! It's so great to see you.
-Hey!

00:00:16.515 --> 00:00:20.186
-Oh, my gosh, thank you so much
for coming on the show.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:21.420
-Happy to be here.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.689
-Oh, it's always good
to see you.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:25.425
Every time we talk,
you've either just finished

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:27.327
or started something
really cool,

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:29.529
either for work or for fun,

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:31.731
but it's always something like,
"Wait, what are you doing?"

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:34.367
You go, "Oh, I'm going to
write a script.

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:36.769
I'm doing a podcast
with Bill Gates."

00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:38.871
Which is unbelievable,
by the way.

00:00:38.871 --> 00:00:40.774
What have you gotten into now?

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:43.075
What is the new interest that
I need to talk to you about?

00:00:43.075 --> 00:00:47.646
-I mean, I wish I could say
it was something epic.

00:00:47.646 --> 00:00:49.649
But it's, like, gardening?

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:51.351
Is that epic?
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:53.319
No, but I'll take that.
That's real.

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:55.655
Gardening?
-It's real. Gardening.

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:58.991
-I love gardening.
I would love to garden.

00:00:58.991 --> 00:01:00.993
How deep do you go?

00:01:00.993 --> 00:01:02.829
Do you change outfits?

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:04.830
-I go deep, I change outfits,

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:09.068
I have, like, a hat, I have
contraptions, I have tools.

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:11.370
-Yes!
-Shovels and things.

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:14.240
-Shears.
-Shears.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.242
Not like "Mommie Dearest" vibes.

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:17.476
Not, like, giant ones
but little guys.

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:18.911
-Oh, yeah, that's, like, hedges,
yeah.

00:01:18.911 --> 00:01:20.980
This is more, like,
those little tiny clippers.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.648
-Yeah, like little herb ones,
yeah.

00:01:22.648 --> 00:01:24.316
-Oh! What do you grow?

00:01:24.316 --> 00:01:26.553
Flowers, herbs?

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:30.390
-Yeah, I grow -- I have a lot
of herbs. I have vegetables.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:32.691
I have a lot of different
kinds of lettuce and kale.

00:01:32.691 --> 00:01:36.762
I grow French snap peas
and chives and basil.

00:01:36.762 --> 00:01:41.167
The crazy thing is that
I have this plant called yarrow

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:44.070
in my garden, and I have
a gardening teacher,

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:47.006
and she was like, "Just so you
know, this stops bleeding."

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:49.108
And I was like, "Okay, alright.

00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:54.013
Whatever witchy magic,
whatever."

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:56.582
-Yeah, I'll have a yarrow.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:56.582 --> 00:01:58.651
Can't wait to stop
the bleeding with the yarrow.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:01.287
And one night, I nicked myself
with a cheese knife.

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:03.422
-Are you kidding me?
I do it every week.

00:02:03.422 --> 00:02:08.127
-Yeah, and I, like,
took the yarrow and I --

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:10.496
Swear to God, I was,
like, pouring blood

00:02:10.496 --> 00:02:12.498
and could not stop.

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:14.567
Was like, you know, holding it
and compressing.

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:15.634
Nothing was working.

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:17.604
And I rubbed it on my cut,

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:19.338
and it immediately stopped,

00:02:19.338 --> 00:02:22.708
and there was, like, a clotting
ring around it like this.

00:02:22.708 --> 00:02:24.443
It was like magic.
Like, it freaked me out.

00:02:24.443 --> 00:02:26.645
-What?! Yarrow?!
-I know. Yarrow.

00:02:26.645 --> 00:02:28.247
-See? This is what --

00:02:28.247 --> 00:02:30.349
I knew, I knew.
You always give me something.

00:02:30.349 --> 00:02:32.151
I love it. Yarrow.

00:02:32.151 --> 00:02:34.086
I'm going to start
growing yarrow.

00:02:34.086 --> 00:02:36.322
-You have to 'cause
that's actually practical.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.624
Like, forget about your palate.

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:41.060
That's medical.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.262
-That's what I'm into.
I love it.

00:02:43.262 --> 00:02:45.698
I have to talk about the baby.

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:48.134
Oh, my gosh, I mean,
he's so cute.

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:52.005
How great is it to get to
spend more time with him?

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:54.340
-It's pretty hilarious.
It's pretty great.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:57.777
I mean, he's really, like, the
only marker of time right now

00:02:57.777 --> 00:03:00.813
'cause everything else is
just, like, so subjective.

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:04.149
But, you know,
he's, like, becoming a person,

00:03:04.149 --> 00:03:06.352
and I get to see the whole
thing, which is awesome.

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:08.053
-I want to know
how musical is the baby

00:03:08.053 --> 00:03:09.722
'cause you come from
a musical family.

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:13.393
Obviously Quincy Jones --
we love Quincy.

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:17.096
Your partner is a musician.

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:19.098
You're musical.

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:20.866
Is he musical?

00:03:20.866 --> 00:03:23.736
-He's not tone deaf.
So that's the good news.

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:24.937
-Oh, I like that.

00:03:24.937 --> 00:03:26.138
-You know what I mean?

00:03:26.138 --> 00:03:28.207
Like, I don't know.
Who knows what will be?

00:03:28.207 --> 00:03:32.344
He has a very good sense
of melody and rhythm.

00:03:32.344 --> 00:03:34.213
He's very into drums.

00:03:34.213 --> 00:03:36.181
I'm gonna call Ahmir.

00:03:36.181 --> 00:03:38.617
-Let's talk about
"On the Rocks."

00:03:38.617 --> 00:03:41.754
You and Bill Murray,
Sofia Coppola?

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:43.690
What?! Dude!

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:45.824
-I guess that's a cool thing
I did, right?

00:03:45.824 --> 00:03:49.562
-What?! Yes! You think so?

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.664
Now it's getting awards buzz.

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:54.433
Yeah, I think it's something
you can talk about.

00:03:54.433 --> 00:03:56.535
Can you tell everyone
what it's about?

00:03:56.535 --> 00:03:59.772
-Yeah. I mean, you know,
it's so weird

00:03:59.772 --> 00:04:01.841
because it's like
instant vintage.

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:06.645
We filmed it last summer,
and we filmed all over New York.

00:04:06.645 --> 00:04:10.216
And it's, you know,
the city's so beautiful in it.

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:12.218
It's such an important part
of the story that, like,

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:15.654
the fact that we did that just
under the wire before lockdown

00:04:15.654 --> 00:04:19.592
is so -- it's like
immediately nostalgic,

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:20.793
which is such a weird thing.

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:23.029
But then it's also
kind of a movie about

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:25.431
a father and a daughter
relationship,

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:27.499
and, you know, that's something
that's very close

00:04:27.499 --> 00:04:29.935
to my heart and Sofia's heart,
obviously, and, like,

00:04:29.935 --> 00:04:33.673
having this sort of, like,
father that changes the energy

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:35.040
of a room when he walks in.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.476
Like, that's something
I'm also very familiar with.

00:04:37.476 --> 00:04:40.479
And then just, like,
navigating that relationship.

00:04:40.479 --> 00:04:43.816
Being an adult through
that relationship is kind of

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:45.284
what the movie is about.

00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:48.688
-Has Quincy or Francis Ford
Coppola seen the movie?

00:04:48.688 --> 00:04:50.322
-Both. Yes.

00:04:50.322 --> 00:04:53.025
-And are they going like,
"That's not me"?

00:04:53.025 --> 00:04:55.094
-Yeah, they're basically like,
"That's Quincy."

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:56.929
"No, that's like Francis."

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:59.165
Like, neither of them are
willing to feel like

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:02.101
they're the inspiration
for the movie, which is great.

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:04.269
-But I mean, but they're like,
"Okay, cool.

00:05:04.269 --> 00:05:07.006
I mean, we're cool,
but Bill Murray's cool."

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:09.541
I mean, Bill is
just the most fun human.

00:05:09.541 --> 00:05:12.077
-The coolest, yeah, yeah,
he's so fun.

00:05:12.077 --> 00:05:14.747
-That car chase, I heard that
sometimes he kind of went

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:17.015
off script and just
started driving around

00:05:17.015 --> 00:05:19.385
where he wasn't supposed to be.

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:23.022
-Yeah. Well, he fancies himself
like an amateur --

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:25.591
Well, probably even more like
a professional stunt driver.

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:28.994
Like, he really prides himself
on doing most of it himself

00:05:28.994 --> 00:05:34.867
and, like, would speak stunt
talk with his stunt double.

00:05:34.867 --> 00:05:38.537
But he did most of the driving
himself, and I think part of it

00:05:38.537 --> 00:05:43.042
was because he likes to -- you
know, he likes to pull a stunt.

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:46.612
He likes to make people scream
and laugh and feel surprised.

00:05:46.612 --> 00:05:50.015
So he would, you know --
We'd finish the scene,

00:05:50.015 --> 00:05:53.085
and then he would just,
like, bolt and, like, lose

00:05:53.085 --> 00:05:57.957
the follow van and all of
our escorts and, like,

00:05:57.957 --> 00:06:02.962
just rip up Tenth Avenue
and get us busted.

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:04.463
He got us busted once.
-No!

00:06:04.463 --> 00:06:06.698
-We were fine because it's him.
Yeah, totally.

00:06:06.698 --> 00:06:08.300
'Cause we saw lights.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:10.035
I was like,
"Bill, we got to go back."

00:06:10.035 --> 00:06:12.839
And I saw lights behind us.
I'm like, "That's not our guys.

00:06:12.839 --> 00:06:14.841
You know those are not the guys
in the production, right?"

00:06:14.841 --> 00:06:16.075
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:16.075 --> 00:06:17.676
-And the guy was like,
"You got to get off --

00:06:17.676 --> 00:06:19.545
What are you doing?
Get off the street."

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:21.113
Luckily we were fine, but --

00:06:21.113 --> 00:06:23.215
-Yeah, you're like,
"That's Bill Murray driving."

00:06:23.215 --> 00:06:25.150
And he's like, "Oh, okay.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:27.219
Let me escort you
back to the set."

00:06:27.219 --> 00:06:30.089
-Exactly.
"Do you need any gas?"

00:06:30.089 --> 00:06:31.891
It's just like the movie.
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:35.628
-He gets away with everything,
that guy.

00:06:35.628 --> 00:06:36.995
-You two together, that's great.

00:06:36.995 --> 00:06:40.199
And Sofia is awesome.

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:41.800
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:45.070
Here's Rashida Jones and
Bill Murray in "On the Rocks."

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:46.405
Take a look at this.

00:06:46.405 --> 00:06:49.341
-What does Dean have planned
for your birthday?

00:06:49.341 --> 00:06:51.711
-He's not going to be here
for my birthday.

00:06:51.711 --> 00:06:55.014
-What kind of guy forgets
his wife's birthday?

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:57.549
-He didn't forget.
He has a work trip.

00:06:57.549 --> 00:06:58.917
But we're going to celebrate
when he gets back.

00:06:58.917 --> 00:07:01.821
-That's not the same.

00:07:01.821 --> 00:07:03.689
I traveled.

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:05.491
I never missed your birthday.

00:07:05.491 --> 00:07:08.694
-Right, but you had
some other shortcomings.

00:07:11.464 --> 00:07:13.099
-Like what?

00:07:17.236 --> 00:07:19.872
-Thank you.

00:07:19.872 --> 00:07:21.474
-Spasibo.

00:07:25.111 --> 00:07:27.747
Alright.
I'm going to take you to 21.

00:07:27.747 --> 00:07:30.016
Just do me a favor
and check his texts, will ya?

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:33.051
-Rashida Jones, everybody.

00:07:33.051 --> 00:07:36.556
"On the Rocks" is streaming now
on Apple TV+.

